    {
      "data": {
        "level": 1,
        "text": "StatCraft Feature Guide (v0.2.2)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661107400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "This document serves as an exhaustive reference of all implemented capabilities, analytical procedures, mathematical algorithms, and user interface features available in the **StatCraft** statistical package."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661110100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661111100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. Dual-View Data Management & Tabular Editors"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661111600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "StatCraft provides a canonical SPSS-style workspace with instantaneous switching between the observational data grid (**Data View**) and the metadata dictionary (**Variable View**)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661112600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "1.1. Data Import & Creation"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661113300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Streaming CSV / TSV Ingest:** High-performance streaming reader with automatic column type inference, configurable field delimiters (comma, semicolon, tab), and decimal point formatting.\n* **Microsoft Excel Import (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.ods`):** Direct workbook reader powered by the open-source Calamine engine, providing automated header sanitization to SPSS naming rules and column type inference.\n* **Blank Dataset Mode (`Blank Dataset`):** Instant instantiation of an empty observation matrix (40 cases by default) for manual tabular data entry without opening external files."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661114700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "1.2. Data View"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661115400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Virtualized Tabular Grid:** Fluid scrolling across tens of thousands of rows and hundreds of columns powered by `ScrollArea::show_rows`.\n* **In-Place Cell Editing:** Direct cell input with `Enter` (navigate down) and `Tab` (navigate right) keys, with automatic delimiter and currency normalization.\n* **Auto-Expanding Rows:** Automatic generation of new blank observations upon entering values into the bottom-most row.\n* **Insert & Delete Cases:** Row context menus and keyboard shortcuts for inserting (`Insert Case`) and deleting (`Delete Case`) observations.\n* **Value Labels Toggle (`1/A`):** Toolbar button for instant toggling between raw numeric codes and human-readable descriptive text labels across the entire grid.\n* **Filter Exclusion Masking:** Diagonal vector strike-through over row number headers for cases excluded by an active sample filter."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661116600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "1.3. Variable View"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661117300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Comprehensive variable metadata dictionary compliant with canonical IBM SPSS Statistics standards:\n* **Name (`Name`):** Strict identifier validation according to SPSS rules (letter start, prohibition of whitespace and special characters).\n* **Type (`Type`):** Full support for all 9 canonical variable types:\n  1. *Numeric* (Standard floating-point / integer numbers);\n  2. *Comma* (Numbers with comma-separated thousands and decimal period);\n  3. *Dot* (Numbers with dot-separated thousands and decimal comma);\n  4. *Scientific* (Exponential notation `1.23E+02`);\n  5. *Date* (Calendar dates formatted as `dd.mm.yyyy`, `yyyy-mm-dd`, etc.);\n  6. *Dollar* (Currency format with `\\$` prefix);\n  7. *Custom Currency* (Configurable user currency formats);\n  8. *String* (Arbitrary text character variables);\n  9. *Restricted Numeric* (Integer values with fixed leading zeros).\n* **Width & Decimals (`Width` & `Decimals`):** Dedicated vector spinners `▲ / ▼` for instant adjustment of column display width and decimal precision.\n* **Variable Label (`Label`):** Descriptive titles displayed in dialog pickers and analytical pivot table headers.\n* **Value Labels (`Values`):** Modal dialog mapping discrete numeric codes to descriptive category labels (e.g., `1 = \"Male\"`, `2 = \"Female\"`).\n* **Missing Values (`Missing`):** Configurable discrete user-missing values (up to 3 distinct codes) and continuous missing ranges (e.g., `90 through 99`).\n* **Alignment (`Align`):** Text and numeric cell alignment (*Left / Center / Right*).\n* **Measurement Scale (`Measure`):** Nominal (*Nominal*), Ordinal (*Ordinal*), and Scale (*Scale*) measurement classifications with authentic vector icons."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661119900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661120900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Dataset Management & Case Manipulations (Data Menu)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661121400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Sort Cases (`Sort Cases`):**\n  * Multi-column stable sorting across an unlimited number of sorting keys.\n  * Independent sorting direction per key: Ascending or Descending.\n  * Strict adherence to SPSS sorting standards: System-missing (`SYSMIS`, `NaN`) values sort first in ascending order and last in descending order.\n* **Select Cases (`Select Cases`):**\n  * Case filtering based on conditional expressions via an integrated modal condition calculator.\n  * Non-destructive filtering mode creating an active binary `filter_$` variable while preserving excluded cases.\n  * Permanent deletion mode for cases not satisfying the filtering condition.\n  * Status bar vector indicator: `Filter: ON (var)`.\n* **Split File (`Split File`):**\n  * Stratified analysis segmented across categorical subgroups (supporting multiple grouping variables).\n  * Modes: *Compare groups* (side-by-side grouped output tables) and *Organize output by groups* (separate sequential output blocks).\n  * Status bar vector indicator: `Split File: ON (var)`.\n* **Weight Cases (`Weight Cases`):**\n  * Frequency and sampling case weighting using values from a designated numeric variable.\n  * Automatic propagation of fractional and integer weights across all descriptive, frequency, and parametric procedures.\n  * Status bar vector indicator: `Weight: ON (var)`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661123600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661124300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Data Transformations (Transform Menu)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661124700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All data transformations are powered by standardized `DialogKit` interfaces, syntax generators, and non-destructive Undo support (`Ctrl+Z`):"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661125500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Compute Variable (`Compute Variable`):**\n  * Computation of new target variables or replacement of existing columns using mathematical expressions.\n  * Built-in Shunting-yard expression parser (Reverse Polish Notation / RPN).\n  * Support for addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, exponentiation (`**`, `^`), and unary operators.\n  * Standard function library: Arithmetic (`ABS`, `EXP`, `LN`, `LOG10`, `RND`, `SQRT`, `TRUNC`) and Statistical (`SUM`, `MEAN`, `MIN`, `MAX`).\n* **Recode into Same Variables (`Recode into Same Variables`):**\n  * In-place value reassignment for selected variables without creating new columns.\n* **Recode into Different Variables (`Recode into Different Variables`):**\n  * Generation of new transformed variables based on conditional recoding rules.\n  * *Old and New Values* subdialog: exact values, continuous ranges (*Range*), open-ended ranges (*Range Lowest through...* / *Range... through Highest*), system- and user-missing values, and fallback rules (*All other values*).\n* **Automatic Recode (`Automatic Recode`):**\n  * Conversion of string or non-contiguous numeric codes into consecutive integers $1, 2, \\dots, K$.\n  * Automatic generation of descriptive value labels preserving source categories.\n  * Direction selection: *Lowest value* or *Highest value*.\n* **Shift Values (`Shift Values`):**\n  * Creation of lagged (*Lag*) and lead (*Lead*) time series columns shifted by $K$ intervals.\n* **Count Values within Cases (`Count Values within Cases`):**\n  * Row-wise counting of occurrences matching specific values or ranges across a list of variables.\n* **Create Dummy Variables (`Create Dummy Variables` / One-Hot Encoding):**\n  * Binary (0/1) indicator generation for categorical scales.\n  * Configurable root names, prefixes, and reference category omission ($k-1$ indicators for linear models).\n* **Random Number Seed (`Set Random Number Seed`):**\n  * Thread-safe global pseudo-random number generator initialization for reproducible sampling and simulations.\n* **Replace Missing Values (`Replace Missing Values`):**\n  * Imputation algorithms: Series Mean, Mean of nearby points, Median of nearby points, Linear interpolation, and Linear trend at point.\n* **Create Time Series (`Create Time Series`):**\n  * First-order differences (`DIFF`), seasonal differences (`SDIFF`), simple moving averages (`SMA`), and cumulative sums (`CSUM`).\n* **Visual Binning (`Visual Binning`):**\n  * Continuous variable discretization: Equal Width intervals, Equal Percentiles (quantiles), and Standard Deviation cutpoints.\n  * Automatic generation of descriptive interval labels (e.g., `< 20`, `20 - 40`, `> 40`).\n* **Optimal Binning (`Optimal Binning`):**\n  * Supervised discretization of continuous predictors against a categorical target using the Fayyad & Irani MDLP entropy algorithm.\n* **Rank Cases (`Rank Cases`):**\n  * Rank assignment with tie handling: Mean (mid-ranks), Low, High, and Sequential.\n  * Rank types: Simple ranks, fractional ranks, percentages, Ntiles, and normal scores (Blom, Tukey, Rankit, Van der Waerden) with Acklam approximation ($\\le 1.15 \\times 10^{-9}$).\n* **Date and Time Wizard (`Date and Time Wizard`):**\n  * Date component extraction: Year, Month, Day, Hour, Minute, Second, Day of week, Quarter.\n  * Calculation of duration between two dates (`DATEDIFF`) in days, months, or years.\n  * Addition or subtraction of time intervals (`DATESUM`).\n* **Automated Data Preparation (`Automated Data Preparation / ADP`):**\n  * Comprehensive pipeline: predictor screening, outlier handling (winsorizing or set to sysmis), feature scaling (Z-score, Min-Max), sparse category merging, pairwise interactions, and validation partitioning.\n* **Programmability Transformations (`Programmability Transformations`):**\n  * Multi-line transformation script editor.\n  * Conditional `IF ... THEN ... ELSE` branching, vector assignments, and real-time syntax validation generating `BEGIN PROGRAM ... END PROGRAM.` blocks."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661136600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661138000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Statistical Procedures (Analyze Menu)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661138500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All statistical algorithms in StatCraft are implemented in **100% pure Safe Rust** and validated against Python `SciPy` and canonical *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* standards to an absolute tolerance threshold of $\\le 10^{-6}$."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661139500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.1. Descriptive Statistics & Cross-Tabulations"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661139900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Descriptives (`Descriptives`):**\n  * Spicer (1972) recurrence moments: Valid $N$, Sum, Mean, Std. Error of Mean, Variance, Std. Deviation, Range, Minimum, Maximum, Skewness (with SE), and Bliss sample excess Kurtosis (with SE).\n* **Frequencies (`Frequencies`):**\n  * Authentic SPSS frequency tables: Counts, Percent, Valid Percent (excluding missings), Cumulative Percent.\n  * Quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$) and custom percentiles computed via the canonical HAVERAGE interpolation standard ($r = p(N+1)$).\n* **Crosstabs (`Crosstabs`):**\n  * Two-way $R \\times C$ contingency tables.\n  * Observed counts, expected counts, unstandardized residuals, row percentages, column percentages, and total percentages.\n  * Pearson Chi-Square ($\\chi^2$), Likelihood Ratio ($G^2$).\n  * Yates continuity correction and two-tailed Fisher's exact test for $2 \\times 2$ tables.\n  * Symmetric association measures: Phi ($\\phi$) and Cramér's $V$."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661141800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.2. Mean Comparisons & Analysis of Variance (Compare Means)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661142600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Means Breakdown (`Means Breakdown`):**\n  * Subgroup descriptive breakdown (Mean, $N$, Variance, Median, Min, Max) across categorical factors.\n  * One-way ANOVA table (Between Groups, Within Groups, Total Sum of Squares, $df$, Mean Squares, $F$-statistic, significance).\n  * Association measures: $\\eta$ (Eta) and $\\eta^2$ (Eta Squared).\n* **One-Sample T-Test (`One-Sample T Test`):**\n  * Student's $t$-test comparing sample mean to a specified reference test value.\n  * Degrees of freedom, two-tailed $p$-value via regularized incomplete beta function, mean difference, and 95% (or custom) confidence interval of the difference.\n* **Independent-Samples T-Test (`Independent-Samples T Test`):**\n  * Two-group comparison with *Define Groups* subdialog.\n  * Automatic Levene's Test for Equality of Variances ($F$, Sig).\n  * Dual-row output table: Student's $t$-test (Equal variances assumed) and Welch's $t$-test (Equal variances not assumed with Satterthwaite fractional degrees of freedom).\n* **Paired-Samples T-Test (`Paired-Samples T Test`):**\n  * Comparison of matched pairs and repeated measures.\n  * Paired statistics, intra-pair Pearson correlation ($r$, Sig), and paired differences test ($t$, $df$, confidence interval).\n* **One-Way ANOVA (`One-Way ANOVA`):**\n  * Fisher's $F$-test comparing multiple treatment groups.\n  * Between-groups and within-groups sums of squares ($SS$) and mean squares ($MS$).\n  * Levene's Test of Homogeneity of Variances.\n  * Group descriptive statistics with 95% confidence intervals."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661144600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.3. Bivariate Correlations (Correlate)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661145400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Bivariate Correlations (`Bivariate Correlations`):**\n  * Pearson linear correlation coefficient ($r$).\n  * Spearman rank-order correlation coefficient ($\\rho$).\n  * Kendall rank-order correlation coefficient ($\\tau_b$) with full tie adjustments ($v_0, v_1, v_2$).\n  * One-tailed and two-tailed significance levels.\n  * Automatic significance flagging (`*` for $p < 0.05$, `**` for $p < 0.01$).\n  * Cross-product deviations and covariances, pairwise and listwise missing exclusion modes."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661146600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.4. Nonparametric Tests (Nonparametric Tests)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661147200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Two Independent Samples (`Two Independent Samples`):**\n  * Mann-Whitney $U$ test, Wilcoxon rank sum $W$.\n  * Pooled mid-ranking with tie adjustment $\\sum(t_i^3 - t_i)$.\n  * Calculation of expected values, adjusted variances, $Z$-score, and asymptotic two-tailed significance.\n* **K Independent Samples (`K Independent Samples`):**\n  * Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test with tie factor correction $H_{adj}$.\n  * Asymptotic significance computed from the $\\chi^2$ distribution with $df = k - 1$.\n* **Two Related Samples (`Two Related Samples`):**\n  * Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test with tie-adjusted variance and continuity correction.\n  * Sign Test with exact two-tailed binomial significance via the beta distribution."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661148700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.5. Linear Regression (Regression)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661149400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Multiple Linear Regression (`Linear Regression`):**\n  * Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) and Weighted Least Squares (WLS) solvers.\n  * *Model Summary* table: Multiple correlation $R$, $R^2$, Adjusted $R^2$, Std. Error of the Estimate.\n  * *ANOVA* table: Regression and residual sums of squares, mean squares, Fisher's $F$, significance.\n  * *Coefficients* table: Unstandardized coefficients $B$ and standard errors, standardized coefficients $\\beta$, $t$-statistics, significance levels, and 95% confidence intervals.\n  * Collinearity diagnostics: Tolerance and Variance Inflation Factor (VIF)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661150800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.6. Scale Reliability Analysis (Scale)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661151500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Reliability Analysis (`Reliability Analysis`):**\n  * Cronbach's Alpha ($\\alpha$) and standardized item alpha.\n  * *Item Statistics*: Mean, standard deviation, and valid $N$ per item.\n  * *Item-Total Statistics*: Scale mean if item deleted, scale variance if item deleted, corrected item-total correlation, Cronbach's alpha if item deleted.\n  * Overall summary *Scale Statistics*."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661152400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.7. Dimension Reduction (Dimension Reduction)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661153200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Factor Analysis & Principal Component Analysis (`Factor Analysis / PCA`):**\n  * Principal Component Analysis via cyclical Jacobi eigensolver for symmetric correlation matrices.\n  * Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy.\n  * Bartlett's Test of Sphericity with exact $\\chi^2$ and significance.\n  * *Communalities* table: Initial and Extraction values.\n  * *Total Variance Explained* table: Eigenvalues, % of variance, and cumulative variance.\n  * Component Matrix showing unrotated factor loadings."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661154400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661155000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Output Management & Clipboard Integration (Output Viewer)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661155400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Interactive Outline Navigation:**\n  * Tree panel on the left reflecting document structure across procedures, syntax logs, and tables.\n  * Smooth scrolling and focus ring highlighting upon selecting any item in the tree.\n  * Synchronized two-way selection: clicking a table in the scroll canvas highlights its node in the outline.\n  * Outline toolstrip: collapse all, expand all, clear entire output, and delete selected nodes with the `Delete` key.\n* **Authentic Pivot Tables:**\n  * High-fidelity reproduction of IBM SPSS Statistics typography and layouts: nested multi-tier headers, alternating row striping, right-aligned numeric formatting, and criterion footnotes.\n* **One-Click Excel TSV Export:**\n  * Dedicated `[ Copy Table (TSV) ]` button in each table header.\n  * Structured Tab-Separated Values (TSV) format engineered for Microsoft Excel and Google Sheets: pastes cleanly with zero column shifting, date corruption, or text truncation.\n* **Syntax Execution Protocols (Log):**\n  * Automatic monospace log blocks documenting executed SPSS syntax (`GET DATA`, `DESCRIPTIVES`, `CROSSTABS`, `REGRESSION`, etc.) with timestamps."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661157200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661157800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "6. SPSS Command Syntax (`.sps`) & Command Bus"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661158400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Typed Command Bus (`CommandBus`):**\n  * Every user action is encapsulated as a typed `EngineCommand` providing parameter schemas for external agents (`specs()`).\n* **Canonical `[ Paste ]` Action:**\n  * Clicking `[ Paste ]` in any modal dialog translates configured parameters into valid SPSS command syntax and directs it into the Syntax Editor or Log.\n* **Syntax Editor:**\n  * Dedicated code editing tab with monospace styling, line execution, and batch processing.\n* **Non-Destructive History (`Undo / Redo`):**\n  * In-memory `DeltaBuffer` transaction engine enabling instant undo/redo of data edits and metadata modifications via `Ctrl+Z` / `Ctrl+Y`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661159900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793994630661160400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "7. AI Readiness (Agent-Ready) & MCP Bridge Status"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793994630661160800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
