<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="generator" content="CapsuleCraft Native"></head><body style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;max-width:720px;margin:32px auto;line-height:1.55;color:#23201c;background:#faf8f4;"><h1>📚 StatCraft / StatCraft Feature Guide (v0.2.2)</h1><p><em>[callout block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><h1>StatCraft Feature Guide (v0.2.2)</h1><p>This document serves as an exhaustive reference of all implemented capabilities, analytical procedures, mathematical algorithms, and user interface features available in the **StatCraft** statistical package.</p><p>---</p><h2>1. Dual-View Data Management &amp; Tabular Editors</h2><p>StatCraft provides a canonical SPSS-style workspace with instantaneous switching between the observational data grid (**Data View**) and the metadata dictionary (**Variable View**).</p><h3>1.1. Data Import &amp; Creation</h3><p>* **Streaming CSV / TSV Ingest:** High-performance streaming reader with automatic column type inference, configurable field delimiters (comma, semicolon, tab), and decimal point formatting.<br>* **Microsoft Excel Import (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.ods`):** Direct workbook reader powered by the open-source Calamine engine, providing automated header sanitization to SPSS naming rules and column type inference.<br>* **Blank Dataset Mode (`Blank Dataset`):** Instant instantiation of an empty observation matrix (40 cases by default) for manual tabular data entry without opening external files.</p><h3>1.2. Data View</h3><p>* **Virtualized Tabular Grid:** Fluid scrolling across tens of thousands of rows and hundreds of columns powered by `ScrollArea::show_rows`.<br>* **In-Place Cell Editing:** Direct cell input with `Enter` (navigate down) and `Tab` (navigate right) keys, with automatic delimiter and currency normalization.<br>* **Auto-Expanding Rows:** Automatic generation of new blank observations upon entering values into the bottom-most row.<br>* **Insert &amp; Delete Cases:** Row context menus and keyboard shortcuts for inserting (`Insert Case`) and deleting (`Delete Case`) observations.<br>* **Value Labels Toggle (`1/A`):** Toolbar button for instant toggling between raw numeric codes and human-readable descriptive text labels across the entire grid.<br>* **Filter Exclusion Masking:** Diagonal vector strike-through over row number headers for cases excluded by an active sample filter.</p><h3>1.3. Variable View</h3><p>Comprehensive variable metadata dictionary compliant with canonical IBM SPSS Statistics standards:<br>* **Name (`Name`):** Strict identifier validation according to SPSS rules (letter start, prohibition of whitespace and special characters).<br>* **Type (`Type`):** Full support for all 9 canonical variable types:<br>  1. *Numeric* (Standard floating-point / integer numbers);<br>  2. *Comma* (Numbers with comma-separated thousands and decimal period);<br>  3. *Dot* (Numbers with dot-separated thousands and decimal comma);<br>  4. *Scientific* (Exponential notation `1.23E+02`);<br>  5. *Date* (Calendar dates formatted as `dd.mm.yyyy`, `yyyy-mm-dd`, etc.);<br>  6. *Dollar* (Currency format with `\$` prefix);<br>  7. *Custom Currency* (Configurable user currency formats);<br>  8. *String* (Arbitrary text character variables);<br>  9. *Restricted Numeric* (Integer values with fixed leading zeros).<br>* **Width &amp; Decimals (`Width` &amp; `Decimals`):** Dedicated vector spinners `▲ / ▼` for instant adjustment of column display width and decimal precision.<br>* **Variable Label (`Label`):** Descriptive titles displayed in dialog pickers and analytical pivot table headers.<br>* **Value Labels (`Values`):** Modal dialog mapping discrete numeric codes to descriptive category labels (e.g., `1 = &quot;Male&quot;`, `2 = &quot;Female&quot;`).<br>* **Missing Values (`Missing`):** Configurable discrete user-missing values (up to 3 distinct codes) and continuous missing ranges (e.g., `90 through 99`).<br>* **Alignment (`Align`):** Text and numeric cell alignment (*Left / Center / Right*).<br>* **Measurement Scale (`Measure`):** Nominal (*Nominal*), Ordinal (*Ordinal*), and Scale (*Scale*) measurement classifications with authentic vector icons.</p><p>---</p><h2>2. Dataset Management &amp; Case Manipulations (Data Menu)</h2><p>* **Sort Cases (`Sort Cases`):**<br>  * Multi-column stable sorting across an unlimited number of sorting keys.<br>  * Independent sorting direction per key: Ascending or Descending.<br>  * Strict adherence to SPSS sorting standards: System-missing (`SYSMIS`, `NaN`) values sort first in ascending order and last in descending order.<br>* **Select Cases (`Select Cases`):**<br>  * Case filtering based on conditional expressions via an integrated modal condition calculator.<br>  * Non-destructive filtering mode creating an active binary `filter_$` variable while preserving excluded cases.<br>  * Permanent deletion mode for cases not satisfying the filtering condition.<br>  * Status bar vector indicator: `Filter: ON (var)`.<br>* **Split File (`Split File`):**<br>  * Stratified analysis segmented across categorical subgroups (supporting multiple grouping variables).<br>  * Modes: *Compare groups* (side-by-side grouped output tables) and *Organize output by groups* (separate sequential output blocks).<br>  * Status bar vector indicator: `Split File: ON (var)`.<br>* **Weight Cases (`Weight Cases`):**<br>  * Frequency and sampling case weighting using values from a designated numeric variable.<br>  * Automatic propagation of fractional and integer weights across all descriptive, frequency, and parametric procedures.<br>  * Status bar vector indicator: `Weight: ON (var)`.</p><p>---</p><h2>3. Data Transformations (Transform Menu)</h2><p>All data transformations are powered by standardized `DialogKit` interfaces, syntax generators, and non-destructive Undo support (`Ctrl+Z`):</p><p>* **Compute Variable (`Compute Variable`):**<br>  * Computation of new target variables or replacement of existing columns using mathematical expressions.<br>  * Built-in Shunting-yard expression parser (Reverse Polish Notation / RPN).<br>  * Support for addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, exponentiation (`**`, `^`), and unary operators.<br>  * Standard function library: Arithmetic (`ABS`, `EXP`, `LN`, `LOG10`, `RND`, `SQRT`, `TRUNC`) and Statistical (`SUM`, `MEAN`, `MIN`, `MAX`).<br>* **Recode into Same Variables (`Recode into Same Variables`):**<br>  * In-place value reassignment for selected variables without creating new columns.<br>* **Recode into Different Variables (`Recode into Different Variables`):**<br>  * Generation of new transformed variables based on conditional recoding rules.<br>  * *Old and New Values* subdialog: exact values, continuous ranges (*Range*), open-ended ranges (*Range Lowest through...* / *Range... through Highest*), system- and user-missing values, and fallback rules (*All other values*).<br>* **Automatic Recode (`Automatic Recode`):**<br>  * Conversion of string or non-contiguous numeric codes into consecutive integers $1, 2, \dots, K$.<br>  * Automatic generation of descriptive value labels preserving source categories.<br>  * Direction selection: *Lowest value* or *Highest value*.<br>* **Shift Values (`Shift Values`):**<br>  * Creation of lagged (*Lag*) and lead (*Lead*) time series columns shifted by $K$ intervals.<br>* **Count Values within Cases (`Count Values within Cases`):**<br>  * Row-wise counting of occurrences matching specific values or ranges across a list of variables.<br>* **Create Dummy Variables (`Create Dummy Variables` / One-Hot Encoding):**<br>  * Binary (0/1) indicator generation for categorical scales.<br>  * Configurable root names, prefixes, and reference category omission ($k-1$ indicators for linear models).<br>* **Random Number Seed (`Set Random Number Seed`):**<br>  * Thread-safe global pseudo-random number generator initialization for reproducible sampling and simulations.<br>* **Replace Missing Values (`Replace Missing Values`):**<br>  * Imputation algorithms: Series Mean, Mean of nearby points, Median of nearby points, Linear interpolation, and Linear trend at point.<br>* **Create Time Series (`Create Time Series`):**<br>  * First-order differences (`DIFF`), seasonal differences (`SDIFF`), simple moving averages (`SMA`), and cumulative sums (`CSUM`).<br>* **Visual Binning (`Visual Binning`):**<br>  * Continuous variable discretization: Equal Width intervals, Equal Percentiles (quantiles), and Standard Deviation cutpoints.<br>  * Automatic generation of descriptive interval labels (e.g., `&lt; 20`, `20 - 40`, `&gt; 40`).<br>* **Optimal Binning (`Optimal Binning`):**<br>  * Supervised discretization of continuous predictors against a categorical target using the Fayyad &amp; Irani MDLP entropy algorithm.<br>* **Rank Cases (`Rank Cases`):**<br>  * Rank assignment with tie handling: Mean (mid-ranks), Low, High, and Sequential.<br>  * Rank types: Simple ranks, fractional ranks, percentages, Ntiles, and normal scores (Blom, Tukey, Rankit, Van der Waerden) with Acklam approximation ($\le 1.15 \times 10^{-9}$).<br>* **Date and Time Wizard (`Date and Time Wizard`):**<br>  * Date component extraction: Year, Month, Day, Hour, Minute, Second, Day of week, Quarter.<br>  * Calculation of duration between two dates (`DATEDIFF`) in days, months, or years.<br>  * Addition or subtraction of time intervals (`DATESUM`).<br>* **Automated Data Preparation (`Automated Data Preparation / ADP`):**<br>  * Comprehensive pipeline: predictor screening, outlier handling (winsorizing or set to sysmis), feature scaling (Z-score, Min-Max), sparse category merging, pairwise interactions, and validation partitioning.<br>* **Programmability Transformations (`Programmability Transformations`):**<br>  * Multi-line transformation script editor.<br>  * Conditional `IF ... THEN ... ELSE` branching, vector assignments, and real-time syntax validation generating `BEGIN PROGRAM ... END PROGRAM.` blocks.</p><p>---</p><h2>4. Statistical Procedures (Analyze Menu)</h2><p>All statistical algorithms in StatCraft are implemented in **100% pure Safe Rust** and validated against Python `SciPy` and canonical *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* standards to an absolute tolerance threshold of $\le 10^{-6}$.</p><h3>4.1. Descriptive Statistics &amp; Cross-Tabulations</h3><p>* **Descriptives (`Descriptives`):**<br>  * Spicer (1972) recurrence moments: Valid $N$, Sum, Mean, Std. Error of Mean, Variance, Std. Deviation, Range, Minimum, Maximum, Skewness (with SE), and Bliss sample excess Kurtosis (with SE).<br>* **Frequencies (`Frequencies`):**<br>  * Authentic SPSS frequency tables: Counts, Percent, Valid Percent (excluding missings), Cumulative Percent.<br>  * Quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$) and custom percentiles computed via the canonical HAVERAGE interpolation standard ($r = p(N+1)$).<br>* **Crosstabs (`Crosstabs`):**<br>  * Two-way $R \times C$ contingency tables.<br>  * Observed counts, expected counts, unstandardized residuals, row percentages, column percentages, and total percentages.<br>  * Pearson Chi-Square ($\chi^2$), Likelihood Ratio ($G^2$).<br>  * Yates continuity correction and two-tailed Fisher&#39;s exact test for $2 \times 2$ tables.<br>  * Symmetric association measures: Phi ($\phi$) and Cramér&#39;s $V$.</p><h3>4.2. Mean Comparisons &amp; Analysis of Variance (Compare Means)</h3><p>* **Means Breakdown (`Means Breakdown`):**<br>  * Subgroup descriptive breakdown (Mean, $N$, Variance, Median, Min, Max) across categorical factors.<br>  * One-way ANOVA table (Between Groups, Within Groups, Total Sum of Squares, $df$, Mean Squares, $F$-statistic, significance).<br>  * Association measures: $\eta$ (Eta) and $\eta^2$ (Eta Squared).<br>* **One-Sample T-Test (`One-Sample T Test`):**<br>  * Student&#39;s $t$-test comparing sample mean to a specified reference test value.<br>  * Degrees of freedom, two-tailed $p$-value via regularized incomplete beta function, mean difference, and 95% (or custom) confidence interval of the difference.<br>* **Independent-Samples T-Test (`Independent-Samples T Test`):**<br>  * Two-group comparison with *Define Groups* subdialog.<br>  * Automatic Levene&#39;s Test for Equality of Variances ($F$, Sig).<br>  * Dual-row output table: Student&#39;s $t$-test (Equal variances assumed) and Welch&#39;s $t$-test (Equal variances not assumed with Satterthwaite fractional degrees of freedom).<br>* **Paired-Samples T-Test (`Paired-Samples T Test`):**<br>  * Comparison of matched pairs and repeated measures.<br>  * Paired statistics, intra-pair Pearson correlation ($r$, Sig), and paired differences test ($t$, $df$, confidence interval).<br>* **One-Way ANOVA (`One-Way ANOVA`):**<br>  * Fisher&#39;s $F$-test comparing multiple treatment groups.<br>  * Between-groups and within-groups sums of squares ($SS$) and mean squares ($MS$).<br>  * Levene&#39;s Test of Homogeneity of Variances.<br>  * Group descriptive statistics with 95% confidence intervals.</p><h3>4.3. Bivariate Correlations (Correlate)</h3><p>* **Bivariate Correlations (`Bivariate Correlations`):**<br>  * Pearson linear correlation coefficient ($r$).<br>  * Spearman rank-order correlation coefficient ($\rho$).<br>  * Kendall rank-order correlation coefficient ($\tau_b$) with full tie adjustments ($v_0, v_1, v_2$).<br>  * One-tailed and two-tailed significance levels.<br>  * Automatic significance flagging (`*` for $p &lt; 0.05$, `**` for $p &lt; 0.01$).<br>  * Cross-product deviations and covariances, pairwise and listwise missing exclusion modes.</p><h3>4.4. Nonparametric Tests (Nonparametric Tests)</h3><p>* **Two Independent Samples (`Two Independent Samples`):**<br>  * Mann-Whitney $U$ test, Wilcoxon rank sum $W$.<br>  * Pooled mid-ranking with tie adjustment $\sum(t_i^3 - t_i)$.<br>  * Calculation of expected values, adjusted variances, $Z$-score, and asymptotic two-tailed significance.<br>* **K Independent Samples (`K Independent Samples`):**<br>  * Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test with tie factor correction $H_{adj}$.<br>  * Asymptotic significance computed from the $\chi^2$ distribution with $df = k - 1$.<br>* **Two Related Samples (`Two Related Samples`):**<br>  * Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test with tie-adjusted variance and continuity correction.<br>  * Sign Test with exact two-tailed binomial significance via the beta distribution.</p><h3>4.5. Linear Regression (Regression)</h3><p>* **Multiple Linear Regression (`Linear Regression`):**<br>  * Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) and Weighted Least Squares (WLS) solvers.<br>  * *Model Summary* table: Multiple correlation $R$, $R^2$, Adjusted $R^2$, Std. Error of the Estimate.<br>  * *ANOVA* table: Regression and residual sums of squares, mean squares, Fisher&#39;s $F$, significance.<br>  * *Coefficients* table: Unstandardized coefficients $B$ and standard errors, standardized coefficients $\beta$, $t$-statistics, significance levels, and 95% confidence intervals.<br>  * Collinearity diagnostics: Tolerance and Variance Inflation Factor (VIF).</p><h3>4.6. Scale Reliability Analysis (Scale)</h3><p>* **Reliability Analysis (`Reliability Analysis`):**<br>  * Cronbach&#39;s Alpha ($\alpha$) and standardized item alpha.<br>  * *Item Statistics*: Mean, standard deviation, and valid $N$ per item.<br>  * *Item-Total Statistics*: Scale mean if item deleted, scale variance if item deleted, corrected item-total correlation, Cronbach&#39;s alpha if item deleted.<br>  * Overall summary *Scale Statistics*.</p><h3>4.7. Dimension Reduction (Dimension Reduction)</h3><p>* **Factor Analysis &amp; Principal Component Analysis (`Factor Analysis / PCA`):**<br>  * Principal Component Analysis via cyclical Jacobi eigensolver for symmetric correlation matrices.<br>  * Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy.<br>  * Bartlett&#39;s Test of Sphericity with exact $\chi^2$ and significance.<br>  * *Communalities* table: Initial and Extraction values.<br>  * *Total Variance Explained* table: Eigenvalues, % of variance, and cumulative variance.<br>  * Component Matrix showing unrotated factor loadings.</p><p>---</p><h2>5. Output Management &amp; Clipboard Integration (Output Viewer)</h2><p>* **Interactive Outline Navigation:**<br>  * Tree panel on the left reflecting document structure across procedures, syntax logs, and tables.<br>  * Smooth scrolling and focus ring highlighting upon selecting any item in the tree.<br>  * Synchronized two-way selection: clicking a table in the scroll canvas highlights its node in the outline.<br>  * Outline toolstrip: collapse all, expand all, clear entire output, and delete selected nodes with the `Delete` key.<br>* **Authentic Pivot Tables:**<br>  * High-fidelity reproduction of IBM SPSS Statistics typography and layouts: nested multi-tier headers, alternating row striping, right-aligned numeric formatting, and criterion footnotes.<br>* **One-Click Excel TSV Export:**<br>  * Dedicated `[ Copy Table (TSV) ]` button in each table header.<br>  * Structured Tab-Separated Values (TSV) format engineered for Microsoft Excel and Google Sheets: pastes cleanly with zero column shifting, date corruption, or text truncation.<br>* **Syntax Execution Protocols (Log):**<br>  * Automatic monospace log blocks documenting executed SPSS syntax (`GET DATA`, `DESCRIPTIVES`, `CROSSTABS`, `REGRESSION`, etc.) with timestamps.</p><p>---</p><h2>6. SPSS Command Syntax (`.sps`) &amp; Command Bus</h2><p>* **Typed Command Bus (`CommandBus`):**<br>  * Every user action is encapsulated as a typed `EngineCommand` providing parameter schemas for external agents (`specs()`).<br>* **Canonical `[ Paste ]` Action:**<br>  * Clicking `[ Paste ]` in any modal dialog translates configured parameters into valid SPSS command syntax and directs it into the Syntax Editor or Log.<br>* **Syntax Editor:**<br>  * Dedicated code editing tab with monospace styling, line execution, and batch processing.<br>* **Non-Destructive History (`Undo / Redo`):**<br>  * In-memory `DeltaBuffer` transaction engine enabling instant undo/redo of data edits and metadata modifications via `Ctrl+Z` / `Ctrl+Y`.</p><p>---</p><h2>7. AI Readiness (Agent-Ready) &amp; MCP Bridge Status</h2><p>* **Parameter Schemas for Agents (`specs()`):**<br>  * Every statistical and data engine procedure (`statcraft_syntax`) provides strongly-typed JSON parameter schemas via `specs()`, allowing external AI agents to validate arguments and construct pipelines headlessly.<br>* **Batch Syntax Scripting:**<br>  * AI assistants can assemble canonical SPSS command syntax (`.sps`) and run it through the engine command bus, yielding complete execution logs and authentic Output Viewer tables.<br>* **Live Network Bridge Status (MCP &amp; IPC Socket):**<br>  * *In Development (`InDev` / Roadmap):* Direct runtime communication over a local IPC socket / embedded MCP server to control the running desktop GUI is currently in active development (the menu entry `Extensions -&gt; MCP Bridge / Copilot` is flagged as `[dev]`). Live socket connectivity will arrive in subsequent roadmap phases.</p><p>---</p><h2>8. Design System, Reliability, and Localization</h2><p>* **Never-Crash Invariant (100% Safe Rust):**<br>  * Complete absence of `unsafe`, `panic!`, `unwrap()`, and `expect()` in non-test code. Malformed data, singular matrices, or division by zero yield typed errors without terminating the application.<br>* **Vector-First User Interface:**<br>  * 100% vector rendering using `ui.painter()` and hardware-rasterized SVGs. Zero Unicode emojis or unsupported glyphs, completely eliminating &quot;tofu&quot; boxes (`□`) across all platforms.<br>* **Zero-Hardcode Localization:**<br>  * 100% of UI strings are externalized into Project Fluent catalogs (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`).<br>  * On-the-fly language switching (English $\leftrightarrow$ Russian) without application restart.<br>* **Multi-Platform Support:**<br>  * Single codebase with verified native binaries for Windows (x64), Linux (x64), and macOS (Apple Silicon ARM64 &amp; Intel x64).</p><p>---</p><h2>9. Roadmap &amp; Features in Development (InDev / Planned)</h2><p>To guarantee complete technical honesty and transparency, the following modules and menu actions are currently under development in v0.2.2 (`MenuItemStatus::InDev`):</p><p>* **Vector Charting (`statcraft_charts`):**<br>  * Interactive Chart Builder, histograms, scatter plots, line charts, boxplots, pie charts, and tabular brushing &amp; linking.<br>* **Runtime AI Network Bridge (`statcraft_bridge`):**<br>  * Local IPC socket and native Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for live bidirectional communication with external LLMs and IDE assistants.<br>* **Report Exporters:**<br>  * Output Viewer export to PDF and LaTeX (v0.2.2 supports one-click TSV for Excel, HTML, and Plain Text).<br>* **Advanced Statistical Procedures (Analyze):**<br>  * General Linear Models (`GLM`: Univariate, Multivariate, Repeated Measures).<br>  * Logistic Regression (Binary, Multinomial) and Curve Estimation.<br>  * Cluster Analysis (*K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering*).<br>  * Survival Analysis (*Life Tables, Kaplan-Meier, Cox Regression*).<br>  * Exploratory Data Analysis (*Explore*) and Case Summaries / Codebook reports.<br>* **Dataset Operations (Data):**<br>  * File Merging (*Merge Files: Add Cases / Add Variables*).<br>  * Data Restructuring (*Restructure*) and Aggregation (*Aggregate*).<br>* **Clipboard &amp; Search Tools (Edit):**<br>  * Global cell Find &amp; Replace, Go to Case / Variable navigation, application Preferences.<br>* **Visual Theming (View):**<br>  * Light / Dark / System theme toggles and display Zoom controls.</p><hr><p style="color:#8a8175;font-size:12px">Exported from CapsuleCraft Native · &lt;doc-statcraft-docs_features_md@capsuleos.local&gt;</p></body></html>

